---
import { href } from '../lib/href';
import LayerProbingTrainingCanvas from './LayerProbingTrainingCanvas.astro';
---

<article class="layer-probing-page" data-layer-probing>
  <nav aria-label="Project navigation">
    <a href={href('/')}>
      <span aria-hidden="true">← </span>Back home
    </a>
    <a
      class="project-source-link"
      href="https://github.com/nitesh-77/Layer-Probing"
      aria-label="View project code on GitHub"
      title="Project code on GitHub"
    >
      <img src={href('/media/brands/github.svg')} width="36" height="36" alt="" />
      <span>GitHub</span>
    </a>
  </nav>
  <header>
    <h1>Layer-Probing</h1>
    <p class="intro">
      I studied how information evolves in the residual streams of DeepSeek and Qwen, using trained
      probes to measure how readable their final predictions become.
    </p>
    <p class="model-context">DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B / Qwen2-7B-Instruct</p>
  </header>
  <section class="experiment" aria-label="Interactive residual stream model">
    <div class="experiment-intro">
      <h2>Reading the residual stream</h2>
      <p>
        The residual stream is the hidden state carried between layers. Each block updates it. A
        trained probe measures how readable the model's final prediction is from that state.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="toolbar">
      <div class="models" role="group" aria-label="Choose model">
        <button data-model="deepseek" aria-pressed="true">
          DeepSeek
        </button>
        <button data-model="qwen" aria-pressed="false">
          Qwen
        </button>
      </div>
      <span class="frozen">28 blocks · frozen model</span>
    </div>
    <div class="stage">
      <canvas
        id="residual-scene"
        aria-label="Schematic 3D model. Drag to rotate; click a block or use the layer slider to choose its residual output."
      ></canvas>
      <span class="annotation" data-anchor="input">
        Prefix
      </span>
      <span class="annotation" data-anchor="teacher">
        Full model prediction
      </span>
      <span class="annotation stream-label" data-anchor="stream">
        Residual stream
      </span>
      <span class="annotation state-label" data-anchor="state">
        Layer <span data-state-layer>22</span>
      </span>
      <span class="annotation" data-anchor="norm">
        Frozen RMS norm
      </span>
      <span class="annotation probe-label" data-anchor="probe">
        <strong>Linear probe · trainable</strong>
      </span>
      <p class="fallback" hidden>
        3D is unavailable in this browser. The layer control and measured results below still work.
      </p>
      <noscript>
        <p class="no-js">
          Enable JavaScript to explore the 3D model. Training and results below remain available.
        </p>
      </noscript>
      <div class="scene-caption">
        <button id="reset-view">Reset view ↗</button>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="inspection">
      <label for="layer">
        Residual after layer <output id="layer-number">22</output>
      </label>
      <input id="layer" type="range" min="1" max="28" value="22" />
      <div class="range-ends">
        <span>1 · first</span>
        <span>28 · last</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="explanation">The probe bypasses later layers; the full model supplies the target.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="training-section" aria-labelledby="probe-training">
    <div class="training-copy">
      <h2 id="probe-training">How I trained the probes</h2>
      <p>
        A forward hook captured one layer’s residual output. On GSM8K reference-solution prefixes, a
        separate linear probe per layer learned the full model’s next-token distribution. Only probe
        weights changed.
      </p>
    </div>
    <LayerProbingTrainingCanvas />
    <p class="training-context">
      Trained on an <strong>AMD Instinct MI300X</strong>, with 256 training questions and 64
      held-out questions per model.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="story-section probe-results-section" aria-label="Results and experiment details">
    <details>
      <summary>Prediction readability across layers</summary>
      <p>
        Both models showed their largest increase in agreement between layers 22 and 23. This
        measures how closely a trained probe matches its own model, not where reasoning begins.
      </p>
      <figure>
        <a
          class="figure-link"
          href={href('/media/layer-probing/deepseek_qwen_probe_comparison.png')}
        >
          <img
            src={href('/media/layer-probing/deepseek_qwen_probe_comparison.png')}
            alt="Original paired comparison of teacher-to-probe KL, excess cross entropy, top-token agreement, and reference-token accuracy for all 28 layers."
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </a>
        <figcaption>
          The saved plots use code indices 0–27. Their jump from index 21 to 22 is layer 22 to 23 in
          the diagram above. Both models used the same questions. Shading resamples held-out
          questions. KL is teacher to probe, despite the original chart's reversed wording.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Residual magnitude and direction changes</summary>
      <figure>
        <a
          class="figure-link"
          href={href('/media/layer-probing/deepseek_qwen_residual_updates.png')}
        >
          <img
            src={href('/media/layer-probing/deepseek_qwen_residual_updates.png')}
            alt="Measured median relative residual updates and direction changes for DeepSeek and Qwen at the final prompt token."
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </a>
        <figcaption>
          Activation size and direction changes at the final formatted prompt token. The plot omits
          the large embedding-to-first-layer transition. These changes do not themselves measure
          reasoning quality.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Seed checks and experiment details</summary>
      <figure>
        <a class="figure-link" href={href('/media/layer-probing/deepseek_qwen_seed_stability.png')}>
          <img
            src={href('/media/layer-probing/deepseek_qwen_seed_stability.png')}
            alt="Three-seed comparison showing each model's largest adjacent agreement increase from code index 21 to 22."
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </a>
        <figcaption>
          The same jump appeared across all six runs. Lines show seed means; shading shows the
          observed range across three seeds.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure>
        <a class="figure-link" href={href('/media/layer-probing/seed_comparison.png')}>
          <img
            src={href('/media/layer-probing/seed_comparison.png')}
            alt="DeepSeek's full-probe seed range and rank-128 probe, with the shared late-layer transition and lower agreement of the smaller readout."
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </a>
        <figcaption>
          A rank-128 probe reduced parameters from 545 million to 20 million. It retained the jump
          but matched late-layer predictions less closely. This control used one seed and the same
          examples.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
      <p>
        The frozen models ran in BF16. I trained independent FP32 affine probes for one epoch with
        learning rate 0.0005, accumulation over four examples, and a 512-token limit. Evaluation
        covered 7,676 supplied solution tokens. Each selected activation passed through the model's
        frozen final RMS normalization.
      </p>
      <p>
        The objective was KL(teacher || probe). A large readout trained on a small sample reflects
        fitting and optimization as well as the representation. Even the last-layer probe must learn
        its weights.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href={href('/media/layer-probing/evidence.json')}>
          Saved measurements, model revisions, and source-file hashes.
        </a>
      </p>
    </details>
  </section>
  <footer>Geometry shows the method, not the shape or motion of measured activations.</footer>
</article>
<script>
  import data from '../data/layer-probing.json';
  import { createResidualScene } from '../lib/layer-probing-scene';

  const canvas = document.querySelector<HTMLCanvasElement>('#residual-scene');
  const slider = document.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('#layer');
  const layerOutput = document.querySelector('#layer-number');
  let model = data.models[0];
  let selectedLayer = 22;
  let scene: ReturnType<typeof createResidualScene> | undefined;

  function update() {
    if (!model || !slider) return;
    slider.value = String(selectedLayer);
    if (layerOutput) layerOutput.textContent = String(selectedLayer);
    const stateLayer = document.querySelector('[data-state-layer]');
    if (stateLayer) stateLayer.textContent = String(selectedLayer);
    canvas?.setAttribute(
      'aria-label',
      `${model.name}. A probe reads the residual after layer ${selectedLayer} of 28. Drag to rotate, or click a block to select its output.`,
    );
    scene?.select(selectedLayer);
  }

  if (canvas && slider) {
    try {
      scene = createResidualScene(canvas, (layer) => {
        selectedLayer = layer;
        update();
      });
    } catch {
      canvas.hidden = true;
      document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.annotation').forEach((label) => {
        label.hidden = true;
      });
      const fallback = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.fallback');
      if (fallback) fallback.hidden = false;
    }
    slider.addEventListener('input', () => {
      selectedLayer = Number(slider.value);
      update();
    });
    document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-model]').forEach((button) =>
      button.addEventListener('click', () => {
        const next = data.models.find((entry) => entry.id === button.dataset.model);
        if (!next) return;
        model = next;
        document
          .querySelectorAll('[data-model]')
          .forEach((item) => item.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(item === button)));
        update();
      }),
    );
    document.querySelector('#reset-view')?.addEventListener('click', () => scene?.reset());
    window.addEventListener(
      'pagehide',
      () => {
        scene?.dispose();
      },
      { once: true },
    );
    update();
  }
</script>
<style>
  :global(html:has([data-layer-probing])) {
    color-scheme: dark;
    --background: #181a1b;
    --text: #e8e6e3;
    --muted: #d4d2ce;
    --active: #7cceef;
    --probe: #f1a28d;
    --secondary: #d4d2ce;
    --rule: #505550;
    --comparison: #6a7e9f;
    --label-halo: #090b0f;
    background: var(--background);
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .stage,
  :global([data-training-figure]) {
    --sans: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Arial, sans-serif;
    --text: #eeeae3;
    --secondary: #a8abb0;
    --active: #7cceef;
    --probe: #f1a28d;
  }
  .layer-probing-page {
    max-width: 1160px;
    margin: auto;
    padding: 30px 38px 45px;
    color: var(--text);
    font-family: 'Fira Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }
  nav {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 15px;
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--secondary);
  }
  a {
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
  button {
    background: none;
    color: var(--secondary);
    border: 0;
    font: inherit;
    cursor: pointer;
    padding: 11px 0;
  }
  button:focus-visible,
  a:focus-visible,
  input:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--active);
    outline-offset: 5px;
  }
  header {
    max-width: 1000px;
    margin: 76px auto 55px;
  }
  h1 {
    font: 700 52.8px/1 var(--sans);
    letter-spacing: normal;
    margin: 0 0 22px;
  }
  header p.intro {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--secondary);
    font:
      italic 28.8px/1.3 Georgia,
      Times,
      serif;
    text-align: left;
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }
  .model-context {
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--secondary);
    margin: 24px 0 0;
    text-align: left;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  .experiment-intro {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto 35px;
  }
  .experiment-intro h2 {
    font: 700 36px/1.15 var(--sans);
    letter-spacing: normal;
    margin: 0 0 18px;
  }
  .experiment-intro p {
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin: 0;
    text-align: left;
    color: var(--secondary);
  }
  .toolbar {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 16px;
    padding-top: 14px;
  }
  .models {
    display: flex;
    gap: 26px;
  }
  .models button {
    font-size: 15px;
  }
  .models button[aria-pressed='true'] {
    color: var(--text);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--text);
  }
  .frozen {
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--secondary);
  }
  .stage {
    position: relative;
    height: 450px;
  }
  #residual-scene {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    touch-action: pan-y;
    cursor: grab;
  }
  #residual-scene:active {
    cursor: grabbing;
  }
  .annotation {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0;
    pointer-events: none;
    font: 14px/1.6 var(--sans);
    color: var(--text);
    text-align: center;
    white-space: nowrap;
    transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
    text-shadow:
      0 0 5px var(--label-halo),
      0 0 10px var(--label-halo);
  }
  .probe-label strong {
    color: var(--probe);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .scene-caption {
    position: absolute;
    bottom: 8px;
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: flex-end;
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--secondary);
  }
  .scene-caption i {
    display: inline-block;
    height: 2px;
    width: 20px;
    background: var(--active);
    vertical-align: middle;
    margin-right: 8px;
  }
  .scene-caption small {
    font-size: 11px;
    margin-left: 8px;
  }
  .inspection {
    width: min(440px, 100%);
    margin: 8px auto 0;
    padding: 10px 0 0;
    font:
      14px/1.6 'Fira Mono',
      monospace;
  }
  .inspection > label {
    display: block;
    text-align: center;
  }
  #layer-number {
    color: var(--text);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  input {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    margin: 15px 0 10px;
    accent-color: #d4d9e1;
    height: 16px;
    cursor: ew-resize;
  }
  .range-ends {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--secondary);
  }
  .explanation {
    font-size: 12px;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--secondary);
    margin: 20px auto 0;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .state-label,
  .stream-label {
    color: var(--active);
  }
  .annotation small {
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--secondary);
  }
  .comparison-label {
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .training-section {
    margin: 70px 0 45px;
  }
  .training-copy,
  .training-context {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }
  .training-copy h2 {
    font: 700 36px/1.15 var(--sans);
    letter-spacing: normal;
    margin: 0 0 20px;
  }
  .training-copy p,
  .training-context {
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--secondary);
  }
  .training-context strong {
    color: #e4bb7a;
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .probe-results-section {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 45px auto 65px;
  }
  details {
    margin: 18px 0;
  }
  summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    padding: 16px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
    font-size: 17px;
  }
  summary:hover,
  summary:focus-visible {
    color: #e4bb7a;
  }
  summary:focus-visible {
    outline-color: #e4bb7a;
  }
  details > p {
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--secondary);
  }
  figure {
    margin: 24px 0 30px;
  }
  figure img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }
  figcaption {
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--secondary);
    margin-top: 12px;
  }
  details a {
    color: var(--text);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
  details p a {
    color: #e4bb7a;
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .eyebrow {
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--active);
  }
  .method h2 {
    font: 500 30px/1.25 var(--sans);
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    margin: 17px 0;
  }
  .method > p:not(.eyebrow) {
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: var(--secondary);
  }
  .method a {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 15px;
    color: var(--active);
    margin-top: 12px;
  }
  footer {
    font-size: 12px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: var(--secondary);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }
  .fallback,
  .no-js {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 40% 10% auto;
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }
  .fallback[hidden],
  canvas[hidden],
  .annotation[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }
  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .layer-probing-page {
      padding: 22px 20px;
    }
    nav {
      font-size: 12px;
    }
    header {
      margin: 48px auto 38px;
    }
    h1 {
      font-size: 38px;
    }
    header p.intro {
      font-size: 23px;
    }
    .model-context {
      font-size: 12px;
    }
    .experiment-intro h2 {
      font-size: 28px;
    }
    .experiment-intro p {
      font-size: 16px;
    }
    .frozen {
      font-size: 11px;
    }
    .models {
      gap: 16px;
    }
    .models button {
      font-size: 14px;
    }
    .stage {
      height: 350px;
    }
    .annotation {
      font-size: 11px;
    }
    .inspection {
      font-size: 13px;
    }
    .range-ends {
      font-size: 10px;
    }
    .training-section {
      margin-top: 50px;
    }
    .training-copy h2 {
      font-size: 28px;
    }
    .training-copy p,
    .training-context {
      font-size: 16px;
    }
    .method h2 {
      font-size: 26px;
    }
    .scene-caption {
      font-size: 11px;
    }
    .scene-caption button {
      font-size: 12px;
    }
  }
</style>
